Cherry clafoutis with Grand Marnier raspberry caramel
4
Cherry clafoutis served with Grand Marnier raspberry caramel.

---
Clafoutis batter
wheat flour|66.5|g
powdered sugar|60|g
almond meal|20|g
eggs|2.5|pcs
semi-skimmed milk|80|ml
double cream|80|ml
cherries|266.5|g

Tin
soft butter|6.5|g
wheat flour (for tin)|6.5|g

Grand Marnier raspberry caramel
powdered sugar|53.5|g
frozen raspberries|80|g
water|55|ml
Grand Marnier|35|ml
powdered sugar (finish)|33.5|g

---
Preheat the oven to 180°C.
In a bowl, mix the almond meal, flour and sugar.
Make a well, break in the eggs and whisk, gradually incorporating the dry ingredients.
Whisk vigorously if needed to remove lumps.
Add the milk and cream while whisking to get a smooth batter.

Butter and flour the tin.
Arrange the washed and stemmed cherries in the bottom.
Pour the clafoutis batter over.
Bake 30 to 35 min at 180°C, until the clafoutis is set and golden.

Make the raspberry caramel: melt the sugar in a pan until blond caramel.
Add the frozen raspberries, Grand Marnier and water.
Cook about 5 min stirring, then let cool.

Turn out the clafoutis warm or cold, dust with powdered sugar.
Serve with the Grand Marnier raspberry caramel.

---
Optionally mix fresh cherries and morello cherries for different flavours.
Grand Marnier can be replaced with Cointreau or another orange liqueur.

---
dessert
clafoutis
cherry
raspberry
grand-marnier
---
Transport|Easy
Réchauffage|Optional (oven or microwave)
Froid|No
Manger|By hand or cutlery
